{
	"name": "Antiquarian",
	"type": "background",
	"img": "icons/commodities/treasure/glass-cube-teal.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p><strong>Ability Score Increases.</strong> +1 to Intelligence and one other ability score.</p><p><strong>Skill Proficiencies.</strong> Investigation and your choice of two of the following: Arcana, Culture, History, Nature, or Religion.</p><p><strong>Language Proficiencies.</strong> You gain proficiency in two languages of your choosing. At least one of these should be an ancient or dead language.</p><p><strong>Suggested Equipment (cost 40 gp).</strong> Scholar’s pack, common clothes.</p><p><em><strong>Feature: </strong></em><strong>Collector’s Eye.</strong> You have spent many long hours around old, dusty tomes, some of which are written in languages long dead. You gain an expertise die to checks made to translate text written in a language that you are not fluent with into Common.</p><p><em><strong>Adventures and Advancement: </strong></em><strong>Knowledge Broker.</strong> As you unearth more and more ancient texts, others begin to take notice of your skills of procurement. Other booksellers may approach you with rare books (magical or otherwise) for trade, or provide you with rumors where such tomes may be found. Black market miscreants may also approach you, hoping to fence a book—and finally get those cultists off their back.</p><p><strong>Connection and Memento.</strong> Roll 1d10, choose, or make up your own.</p><p>@Embed[Compendium.a5e.a5e-roll-tables.RollTable.AGHFpAg92Z3cVQHg caption=false cite=true rollable=true]</p><p>@Embed[Compendium.a5e.a5e-roll-tables.RollTable.lBwofJKahDAbPnLB caption=false cite=true rollable=true]</p>",
